{
  "id": 409453902,
  "iid": 21017,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "C12.22: Avoid UB if no base OID is given.",
  "description": "At initialization, the C1222 dissector reads a preference string to determine a\nbase OID, but the base OID remains as NULL (with length 0) if the preference\ndoesn't exist or is incorrectly formatted.  It then subsequently \"memcpy\"s that\nbase OID during packet dissection.  My system headers declare memcpy with the\nnonnull attribute on its pointer arguments, so UBSAN complains -- even though\nthe size to copy is zero.\n\nIt's easy enough to simply skip the memcpy if no valid base OID was specified.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2025-08-24T06:57:08.785Z",
  "updated_at": "2025-08-29T04:40:39.146Z",
