    },
    {
      "id": "d5dfd29e1ace64902edeaeb850c9f8d72dcbe412",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2705186708,
          "type": null,
          "body": "(Also it looks like we compile with `-fno-delete-null-pointer-checks`, which avoids the issue of gcc seeing that memcpy was called, assuming that the inputs *can't* be NULL because of that, and then deleting subsequent NULL pointer checks: https://developers.redhat.com/articles/2024/12/11/making-memcpynull-null-0-well-defined#motivation)",
          "author": {
